ns that $1$ is taken as a factor $12$ times. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{1}^{12}={{1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1}_{⏟}}_{12\\text{ times}}=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429895 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429895 #edb/ref 1069 "q-224135" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429895 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429895 #edb/ref 1071 "${4}^{1}=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429895 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "49d63c61-4b5e-531a-8049-3028c80de021" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429895 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, ${4}^{1}$ is in exponent form. The base is $4$ and the exponent is $1.$ \n\nThis means that $4$ is taken as a factor only once. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{4}^{1}=4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429896 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429896 #edb/ref 1069 "q-224152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429896 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429896 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the square of $3?$\n\nThe square of $3$ is\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429896 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "55110545-b3e1-5cf7-8175-0d77be4e9f01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429896 #edb/ref 1074 "The square of $3$ is the same as ${3}^{2}.$\n\nTo evaluate ${3}^{2},$ we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2}={{3\\times 3}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}=9\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429897 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429897 #edb/ref 1069 "q-55034" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429897 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429897 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $9$ raised to the power of $3?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429897 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "67f4609a-bf5e-5370-a6dc-848f8c2f3fef"